2026-10-23T10:10:53.3322388Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3322819Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3322977Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3323200Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3323330Z Commands:
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3323764Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3324457Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3325470Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3326248Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3326949Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3327636Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3328254Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3328934Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3329906Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3330465Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3330994Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3331484Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3331974Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3332416Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3332689Z 
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3332792Z Options:
2026-10-23T10:10:53.3333135Z       --json               Emit machine-readable JSON to stdout; logs remain on stderr
